  "description": "The proposed works are to a palm. It is our understanding, per the online guidance of the Royal Horticultural Society, that a palm is not botanically a tree (see https://www.rhs.org.uk/plants/types/trees/palms-exotic). On that basis, the relevant legislation does not apply and we are not required to provide notice of our proposed works to the palm. We have sought guidance from Wandsworth council to confirm this is the position the council takes as well, but while we await a response, we are providing six weeks' prior notice of our intention to cut down the palm in our back garden of 8 Okeburn Rd. We may withdraw the notice if it is confirmed by the council that it is not required. We propose to cut down the palm entirely and remove the stump. The palm is not visible from the street, is not a native species, and is very close to the house which we consider unsafe. It is a nuisance, and we have received complaints from our neighbours as it overshadows their garden. It is frankly a blight on the conservation zone and an eye sore.",
